WHAT: Raises speed inliner growth budget from 320 to 640, and per-caller
growth from 64 to 128.

WHY: After handler inlining (step 21) created larger caller functions, the
growth budget was being exhausted before all beneficial inlining could occur.

GAS IMPACT: None on any contract.

TEAM NOTES: The growth budget wasn't the bottleneck. Despite doubling the
budget, no additional functions were inlined. The remaining uninlined
functions are either too large or the cost model correctly rejects them.
